    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get the caution, but we're talking about a massive economic engine here. If we start stalling every project because of \"potential\" litigation or \"residual\" risks that are standard in modern construction, nothing ever gets built in this city. \n\nIf I were to tell the council that the geological data doesn't present a *critical* structural threat—just a standard engineering requirement—would that be an accurate reflection of the technical reality, or would I be overstepping?",
